*Observations:*

the values of the turnaround time >100s seems to be very close to the maximum value of the unsigned Integer: 4294967295, might be just coincidence yet makes to believe it might have something to do with the variable type casting.

 

Example high precision turnaround time seems to report proper values.

 
{code:java}
void clientHttpRequest::calculateHighPrecisionTurnaroundTime(uint64_t ts)
{
  al->high_precision_turnaround_time = colib::ticks2Us(ts - al->req_end_tsc_ticks);
}{code}
 

Some old bugzilla (yet for the f line) around similar topic:

[https://bugzilla.akamai.com/show_bug.cgi?id=2857278]

 

*Ask:*

what's the reason behind oddly, unrealistic high turnaround time values?

can we fix it somehow?

